---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { url } from '../lib/paths';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="About Best OutDoor Wears"
  description="Best OutDoor Wears makes a simple, focused layering and packing system for casual hikers and campers — no gear-review clutter, just what to wear and pack."
  canonicalPath="/about/"
>
  <section>
    <div class="wrap prose legal-page" style="max-width:74ch; padding-top:20px;">
      <h1>About Best OutDoor Wears</h1>
      <p>
        Best OutDoor Wears exists for one reason: most outdoor clothing advice is written for people who already
        know what they're doing, or it's a thinly disguised gear catalog. We wanted a resource that starts from
        the actual beginner question — "what do I wear, for this specific trip?" — and answers it directly,
        before pointing you toward gear at all.
      </p>
      <h2>What we focus on</h2>
      <p>
        Everything on this site is organized around one system: layering (base, mid, shell) applied to real trip
        types — day hikes, overnight backpacking, car camping, cold-weather trips, and wet-weather trips. We
        built <a href={url('/product/')}>TrailReady</a> because we kept writing the same trip-specific breakdown for
        friends and decided to put it in one place.
      </p>
      <h2>What we don't do</h2>
      <p>
        We don't publish fabricated reviews, invented statistics, or "tested by thousands of hikers" claims we
        can't back up. Where we reference outdoor clothing brands or affiliate programs, that's disclosed on our
        <a href={url('/affiliate-disclosure/')}>affiliate disclosure page</a>. Product mentions are described as
        commonly recommended options based on how the layering system works, not as personal field tests unless
        stated otherwise.
      </p>
      <h2>Questions?</h2>
      <p>Reach out any time through our <a href={url('/contact/')}>contact page</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
